{"author":{"id":"aefab16712695e4f092f7bad7c1285ac48ce0d1ef6cc283cea20b3795ed9457a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790146254,"nonce":"9v8mCSB2FmbaaO4Bpi6m4+NlsZQ=","title":"[Collab Bug] read-only review task owner cannot close its task because the close gate requires a merge","message":"### Intake Contract\n```json\n{\n  \"acceptance\": [\n    \"a read-only review task can be closed by its owner after the verdict is returned, without a merge commit and without a master force close\",\n    \"existing implementation-task close semantics (merge required) stay unchanged\",\n    \"test proves a review-only owner closes successfully and that stale delivered review tasks no longer accumulate\"\n  ],\n  \"classification\": \"bug\",\n  \"evidence_links\": [\n    \"msg m1790146071717-854\",\n    \"task-scheduler-review-a5dd5b3-e7edb91\",\n    \"task-m1790144140549-824 force close receipt cleanup-manual-task-m1790144140549-824-1790145435463\"\n  ],\n  \"original_input\": \"A managed subagent assigned a read-only review task cannot close that task after returning a verdict. `collab task close \u003creview-task\u003e` is refused with 'task ... must be merged by its owner before close (current: delivered)', and `collab task close --force` is refused with 'manual force close is not authorized for this caller'. A read-only review has no merge of its own, so the owner can never satisfy the merge gate; the live master must force-close every review task, and each force close records cleanup result 'unverified'. Observed on task-scheduler-review-a5dd5b3-e7edb91 and earlier on review tasks task-m1790144140549-824, 177293a-review-f28743d, task-m1790140843992-765. Desired: read-only review tasks close through the normal path (for example a review-terminal status that does not require a merge commit), so the owner ends its own lifecycle without a master force close and without leaving delivered review tasks.\",\n  \"owner\": \"collab::task_lifecycle review close gate\",\n  \"parent_id\": null,\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"collab task close merge gate for read-only review tasks\",\n    \"collab task review/integrated lifecycle for review-only owners\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"open\"\n}\n```\n\n### Original Input\nA managed subagent assigned a read-only review task cannot close that task after returning a verdict. `collab task close \u003creview-task\u003e` is refused with 'task ... must be merged by its owner before close (current: delivered)', and `collab task close --force` is refused with 'manual force close is not authorized for this caller'. A read-only review has no merge of its own, so the owner can never satisfy the merge gate; the live master must force-close every review task, and each force close records cleanup result 'unverified'. Observed on task-scheduler-review-a5dd5b3-e7edb91 and earlier on review tasks task-m1790144140549-824, 177293a-review-f28743d, task-m1790140843992-765. Desired: read-only review tasks close through the normal path (for example a review-terminal status that does not require a merge commit), so the owner ends its own lifecycle without a master force close and without leaving delivered review tasks.\n\nClassification: bug\n\nScope:\n- collab task close merge gate for read-only review tasks\n- collab task review/integrated lifecycle for review-only owners\n\nOwner: collab::task_lifecycle review close gate\nParent: none\n\nAcceptance:\n- a read-only review task can be closed by its owner after the verdict is returned, without a merge commit and without a master force close\n- existing implementation-task close semantics (merge required) stay unchanged\n- test proves a review-only owner closes successfully and that stale delivered review tasks no longer accumulate\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence links:\n- msg m1790146071717-854\n- task-scheduler-review-a5dd5b3-e7edb91\n- task-m1790144140549-824 force close receipt cleanup-manual-task-m1790144140549-824-1790145435463","files":null}]}